---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site, TITLE_MAX } from "../lib/site";
const TITLE = "Privacy — what Utility Helpers counts and what it never sees";
const DESC = "Tool input never leaves your device. With consent we count which tools and buttons get used; Reject and we get nothing. Ads come from Google AdSense.";
const body = `    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Every tool runs in your browser. What you type, paste, generate or convert
    never leaves your device. If you allow it, we count how the tools are used so we know
    which ones to improve and which ones nobody needs.</p>
    <div class="prose">
    <p>Your current choice: <strong data-uh-consent-state>not chosen yet</strong>.
    <span data-uh-js hidden><button type="button" class="linkbtn" data-uh-consent-open>Change your privacy choices</button></span></p>

    <h2>The three choices</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Choice</th><th scope="col">What we receive</th><th scope="col">What is stored in your browser</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Reject</td><td>Nothing.</td><td>Only the fact that you chose Reject (and a light/dark theme, if you switch it yourself).</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Essential only</td><td>Anonymous usage events (listed below) with a random session id that is
          forgotten when you close the tab.</td><td>Your choice, plus the per-tab session id.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Accept all</td><td>The same events, plus a random visitor id so we can see whether people come
          back and which tools they use together.</td><td>Your choice, the session id and
          the random visitor id.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>These choices cover our own usage counts. Ads are run by Google and have their own
    consent step (see <a href="#ads">Ads</a> below). None of our usage counts are sent before you choose. You can change your mind at any time from the
    &ldquo;Privacy choices&rdquo; link at the bottom of every page; switching to Reject or
    Essential only deletes the visitor id from your browser.</p>

    <h2>What a usage event contains</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Which page was opened and which tool was used.</li>
      <li>Which options were picked (for example a unit pair, a text case, a password length).</li>
      <li>Which buttons were pressed (for example Copy, Format, Encode) and whether the tool showed an error.</li>
      <li>How long the page was visible.</li>
      <li>A rough device class: mobile, tablet or desktop.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we never collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Anything you type, paste or get back from a tool: text, JSON, passwords, URLs, colours, dates.</li>
      <li>Your name, email or any account. There are no accounts.</li>
      <li>Your IP address, browser fingerprint or user agent. Our code never stores them; the only device detail is mobile, tablet or desktop.</li>
      <li>Data for anyone else. There are no third-party analytics scripts. The only third party
      is Google AdSense, which shows the ads (see below).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="ads">Ads</h2>
    <p>The site is kept free by Google AdSense, so pages that show tools also load Google&rsquo;s ad
    script. We never pass anything you type into a tool, or its result, to Google or anyone
    else. The ad script is Google&rsquo;s own code and is governed by Google&rsquo;s policies.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your earlier
      visits to this site and to other websites.</li>
      <li>Google&rsquo;s advertising cookies let Google and its partners show you ads based on
      those visits. Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google
      uses information from sites that use its services</a> and
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">how Google uses advertising cookies</a>.</li>
      <li>You can turn off personalised ads in
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/">Google&rsquo;s Ads Settings</a>, or opt out of some
      other vendors&rsquo; cookies at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/">aboutads.info</a>.</li>
      <li>If you are in the European Economic Area, the UK or Switzerland, Google shows its own
      consent message before ads use cookies or personal data, and you can change that choice
      later from the same message.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Your choice in our own banner does not switch ads on or off: it only controls our usage
    counts. Google&rsquo;s cookies can be cleared in your browser settings at any time.</p>

    <h2>Where it goes and for how long</h2>
    <p>Events go to a small first-party function on this site and are stored in the site&rsquo;s own
    storage on Netlify, our host. Raw events are deleted after 90 days. We keep only
    aggregated counts, such as &ldquo;Word Counter was used 120 times this week&rdquo;.</p>

    <h2>Kept only in your browser</h2>
    <p>A light/dark theme you pick and the list of tools you used recently are saved in your
    browser&rsquo;s local storage so the site can remember them (the recent list is not kept if you
    choose Reject). Text or a file you drop on the home
    page is read on that page only and, if you open a tool from there, handed to it inside the same
    tab. None of this is ever sent to us.</p>

    <h2>Suggestions</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/suggest/">suggestion form</a> is separate from the choices above: it sends only
    what you write in it, plus the kind of suggestion and the tool it is about. Please leave
    personal details out. Suggestions are read by the people deciding what to build next.</p>
    <p>To stop the form being flooded, each submission is counted against a one-way hash of
    your IP address mixed with a secret value and the current date. The hash cannot be turned
    back into your IP, is never stored with your suggestion, and is deleted after 2 days.
    Your IP address itself is never stored.</p>

    <h2>The code</h2>
    <p>The site is open source. You can read exactly what is sent in
    <a href="${site.github}/blob/master/public/assets/site.js" rel="noopener">public/assets/site.js</a> and
    <a href="${site.github}/blob/master/netlify/lib/core.mjs" rel="noopener">netlify/lib/core.mjs</a>.</p>
    </div>`;
---
<Base title={TITLE.slice(0, TITLE_MAX)} description={DESC} path="/privacy/">
  <Fragment set:html={body} />
</Base>
